s plausible, and automatic closure based only on inactivity could disrupt legitimate collaboration.","remediation":"Explicitly describe the GitLab maintenance behavior in the skill's activation criteria. Require user approval of the target project and proposed mutations, use least-privilege credentials, and present inactive merge requests for review rather than automatically closing them.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.94},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":14,"end_line":16}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-3b4cdf9768f04665a4e4e982924c323d","category":"Output Handling","pattern":"The workflow publishes findings and closes existing merge requests without warning about privacy or collaboration impacts.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":14,"end_line":16},"finding":"The workflow publishes findings and closes existing merge requests without warning about privacy or collaboration impacts.","explanation":"The instruction to publish learned findings and ideas does not constrain their source or require review for confidential information before sending them to GitLab. This could expose private session or project information to repository viewers, while closing older merge requests without checking their ongoing relevance could disrupt work; these risks overlap with SDI-1.","remediation":"Limit published material to explicitly authorized project information, check drafts for secrets and private context, and confirm repository visibility and audience before submission. Require approval of the final merge-request content and each proposed closure, including a review of current discussion and status.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.92},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":14,"end_line":16}]